# The `|| true` calls are inside the `#DEBHELPER#` block that
# dh_installsystemd generates, not hand-written here, and they are deliberate: a
# unit that cannot be unmasked or enabled on a system not running systemd must
# not make the install fail. This is the standard shape for any package using
# dh_installsystemd.
maintainer-script-ignores-errors

# The project ships no man page, so this package has none. README.Debian says
# where the packaging-specific documentation is installed instead, which is
# /usr/share/doc/ananicy-rs/. The upstream Markdown under docs/ is deliberately
# not installed at all: it is written for people working on the daemon rather
# than for people running it, and it stays in the source package. Writing a man
# page inside the packaging would create a second copy of the command-line
# reference to keep in step with the binary; it belongs upstream, next to the
# code it documents, and that is a change to propose rather than one to smuggle
# in via a recipe.
no-manual-page

# Expected for a package that has never been uploaded: there is no bug to close
# on the initial upload. It goes away by itself once there is an upload behind
# this one.
initial-upload-closes-no-bugs
